<decision #generic-agent-execution-contract apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKV>
  Where should complete AIAgentDefinition execution semantics live in Eidolon?
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKV>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKW>
  Use one optional pure-data contract on the generic AgentConfig/actor snapshot.
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKW>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "generic-contract" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKX>
      Generic actor contract
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKX>
      <description ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKY>
      All actors can carry the same schema, policy and input facts.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKY>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKZ>
      Generic runtime gains a bounded additive contract.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJKZ>
    )>
    <option { key = "workflow-actor" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM0>
      Workflow-specific actor
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM0>
      <description ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM1>
      Create another actor/provider/session implementation.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM1>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM2>
      Duplicates the common runtime and violates the mission boundary.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM2>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM3>
    The user requires reuse of Eidolon common mechanisms.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM3>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM4>
    Complete Agent execution SHALL be represented as an additive generic AgentExecutionContract and persisted in ordinary actor snapshots.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM4>
    <rationale ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM5>
    Schema, exact tools and output validation are agent semantics, not workflow substrate semantics.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM5>
    <evidence ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM6>
    Current DelegateActor, AgentConfig, actor snapshots and WorkflowAgentExecutionFact.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM6>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM7>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM7>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM8>
  moderate
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM8>
)>

<decision #explicit-agent-task-integration apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM9>
  How do Ctrl and Data workflows select an AIAgentDefinition?
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJM9>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMA>
  Use the existing explicit ai.agent effect and exact task tuple from ordinary profile nodes.
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMA>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "ordinary-node-effect" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMB>
      Ordinary node plus explicit effect
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMB>
      <description ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMC>
      Run and TransformNode call the same typed effect.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMC>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMD>
      Flow code remains responsible for explicit selection.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMD>
    )>
    <option { key = "agent-task-node" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJME>
      New AIAgentTask node
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJME>
      <description ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMF>
      Add a new substrate grammar node.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMF>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMG>
      Conflicts with WorkCtrlFlow and duplicates the existing task reference.
      </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMG>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMH>
    depa already defines the task as a four-field resource selection contract.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMH>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMJ>
    AICtrlWorkflow Run and AIDataWorkflow TransformNode SHALL invoke the same ai.agent effect with an exact agentDefinitionRef and payload; no AIAgentTask substrate node is introduced.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMJ>
    <rationale ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMK>
    This preserves substrate generality and shares one host execution path.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMK>
    <evidence ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMM>
    depa Flow DSL and existing EidolonWorkflowEffectProvider.
    </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMM>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMN>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMN>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMP>
  low
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMP>
)>

<decision #closed-effect-policy apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMQ>
  How should EffectPolicy control tool exposure?
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMQ>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMR>
  Support only declared-only and none with exact ToolRefs.
  </?01M0QPCXADKVHDQK5Y0QDAMJMR>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "closed-modes" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRV>
      Closed policy modes
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRV>
      <description ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRW>
      Tool admission follows exact typed resource facts.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRW>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRX>
      New modes require explicit depa and host revisions.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRX>
    )>
    <option { key = "text-policy" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRY>
      Interpret policy text
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRY>
      <description ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRZ>
      Infer tool behavior from names or prose.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PRZ>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS0>
      Creates prohibited fuzzy semantic routing.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS0>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS1>
    Semantic routing must never rely on text matching in code.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS1>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS2>
    The host SHALL implement only exact declared-only and none modes and SHALL reject unsupported or conflicting policy facts.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS2>
    <rationale ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS3>
    Closed values are auditable and deterministic.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS3>
    <evidence ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS4>
    User architecture constraint and depa EffectPolicy projection.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS4>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS5>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS5>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS6>
  moderate
  </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS6>
)>

<decision #result-validation-seam apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS7>
  Where must output schema validation occur?
  </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS7>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS8>
  At the shared generic child completion seam before any success delivery.
  </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS8>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "common-completion" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS9>
      Common completion seam
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PS9>
      <description ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSA>
      Immediate and orchestrated paths share one validator.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSA>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSB>
      Requires a careful common-runtime change.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSB>
    )>
    <option { key = "workflow-postprocess" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSC>
      Workflow-only postprocess
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSC>
      <description ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSD>
      Validate after effect success in workflow code.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSD>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSE>
      Invalid output may already have escaped and other actors diverge.
      </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSE>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSF>
    Validation must precede durable success and result delivery.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSF>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSG>
    Output validation SHALL occur in the common actor completion path before parent tool results, workflow completed events or success facts are written.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSG>
    <rationale ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSH>
    This is the only seam shared by immediate, orchestrated and resumed execution.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSH>
    <evidence ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSJ>
    DelegateActor/result delivery and workflow effect lifecycle.
    </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSJ>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSK>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSK>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSM>
  moderate
  </?01M0QPCXAE43BWA49VX25B5PSM>
)>
